Do not offer WebSockets over HTTP/2 (RFC 8441 extended CONNECT).

Browsers then open WebSockets on their own HTTP/1.1 connection, as with the Go server: video does not share
a TCP connection (and its head-of-line blocking) with API calls, and large messages need no splitting into
HTTP/2 frames, which lws leaves to the application. The h2 settings an application may set do not reach
this one.

--- a/lib/sansio/h2/ops-h2.c
+++ b/lib/sansio/h2/ops-h2.c
@@ -93,7 +93,7 @@
 	 * max_http_header_data.
 	 */
 	/* H2SET_RESERVED7 */				   0,
-	/* H2SET_ENABLE_CONNECT_PROTOCOL */		   1,
+	/* H2SET_ENABLE_CONNECT_PROTOCOL */		   0,
 }};
 
